1986	2129	National political career
Bonino was elected to the Italian Chamber of Deputies in 1976 and reelected in 1979, 1983, 1987, 1992, 1994 and 2006.
2130	2283	In 1975, she founded the Information Centre on Sterilisation and Abortion and promoted the referendum which led to the legalisation of abortion in Italy.
2284	2432	In 1986, she was among the promoters of a referendum against nuclear energy that led to the rejection of a civil nuclear energy programme in Italy.

2432	2536	On 17 May 2006, Bonino was appointed as minister for international trade in the cabinet of Romano Prodi.
2537	2648	She resigned from office on 7 May 2008 when she had been elected vice president of the Senate the previous day.
2649	2837	In 2008, at the elections of 13 and 14 April, she was elected to a seat in the Senate, the second parliamentary chamber, on the list of the Democratic Party for the Piedmont constituency.

2837	2931	On 28 April 2013, she was sworn in as foreign minister in the government led by Enrico Letta.

2931	3040	In June 2017, public opinion polls of her stood at 43 percent, second only to prime minister Paolo Gentiloni.
3041	3150	Despite the positive public opinion, her party fell short of the 3 percent required for a seat in Parliament.
